## Agent Roles & Workflow

```
{% if tool.name == 'claude' %}planner -> (developer-phoenix-backend)? -> (developer-phoenix-frontend)? -> [dev-gate.sh hook] -> reviewer-phoenix -> committer
{% else %}planner -> (developer-phoenix-backend)? -> (developer-phoenix-frontend)? -> [gate] -> reviewer-phoenix -> committer
{% endif %}```

- **planner**: reads codebase, writes structured plan to session log `## Plan` incl. `## Slices` list (Opus — deep analysis)
- **developer-phoenix-backend**: reads `## Plan`, implements schemas/migrations/seeds, contexts/business-logic/Oban/mailers/controllers for `backend` slice (incl. data layer)
- **developer-phoenix-frontend**: reads `## Plan`, implements LiveView render/HEEx/JS hooks/Tailwind/browser tests for `frontend` slice
- **reviewer-phoenix**: reviews Phoenix/Elixir quality/patterns/architecture, reports issues
- **committer**: receives task summary from orchestrator, analyzes git diff, crafts why-focused commit msg, stages and commits (Haiku — cheap and fast)

Subagent rules baked into each agent's system prompt via Jinja `{% include %}` in `.md.j2` templates — subagents do NOT re-read at session start. Delegation prompts only name conditional rules (domain context, stack-specific) for subagent to Read on demand.

## Routing per Slice

Orchestrator reads `## Slices` from planner's plan. Delegates per slice in order:

- `backend` → `developer-phoenix-backend` (includes data layer: schemas, migrations, seeds)
- `frontend` → `developer-phoenix-frontend`

Backend runs before frontend by default; frontend treats files modified by backend as constraints.

## Workspace Rules

- Work in current directory only (never `../`)
- No worktrees — commit directly to main
- Planner (Phase 0) always runs before dev subagent

